{"kind":"event","event_id":7239,"event_uid":"01M2NT1Z8K65QEM0F722CJVJT7","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":308,"issue_uid":"01M2NSXXERXKHW20GJ0TPEAS8Y","issue_short_id":"as8y","actor":"exam:1@run-23","hlc_physical_ms":1789585849619,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"0367b01284d13916bb58a5e97332d854cd3ce9baf7bc28b92f845a0b523c731c","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NT1Z8HAH0C5BZGPSHC4GJ6","author":"exam:1@run-23","body":"examiner (round 1): writing the two exam files the Proof names.\n\nPlan, leg by leg:\n- `tests/state-exams/exam-page.test.ts` — leg (a) [M1] over a plain `globalThis.window` (the shape of `client/test/todos-store.test.ts` leg (e)): flag true -> `readExamFlag()` true and `createTodosStore()` is `toBe` `window.__TINYAPP_STORE__`; `{}` -> false and the handle undefined; window deleted -> false, no throw; `{}` + seed -> handle's `getContent()` deep-equals the two-open-todos content. Window restored in a `finally`. The module is imported as a namespace (`import * as sd`) so that at BASE the missing `readExamFlag` fails its own leg rather than failing the whole file to link, leaving legs (d) and (e) readable. Leg (d) [M4] is the one `stateExam({…})`, spelled exactly as the Proof gives it. Leg (e) [M5] asserts the two `sed | grep` patterns over AGENTS.md's Key Files section and spawns the `bun test` over the two BASE render exams, expecting exit 0.\n- `client/test/exam-page.test.ts` — legs (b) and (c) [M2, M3] in the shape of `client/test/seeded-store-global.test.ts`: register a window only if none is registered, `mock.module` `../src/sqlite` (one sentinel `db` object), both TinyBase link factories and `reconnecting-websocket` before the dynamic imports, count sockets/getDb/synchronizers in module-level counters, render `Provider` + `Store` + a `useStore(STORE_ID)` probe, settle 300 ms, blank `globalThis.happyDOM` before `unregister()` in `afterAll`. Four renders: flagged unseeded (load resolves), flagged unseeded (load never resolves), unflagged unseeded, flagged seeded. Counters read as before/after deltas since the process is shared.","created_at":"2026-09-16T19:10:49.617391756Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T19:10:49.619Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7247,"event_uid":"01M2NT37YRJWJF1X6H69ZK9B61","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":308,"issue_uid":"01M2NSXXERXKHW20GJ0TPEAS8Y","issue_short_id":"as8y","actor":"impl:1@run-23","hlc_physical_ms":1789585891288,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"6dbb2bae426648c6d501e15dc19b9107c67c41b8c0df21c5b57a0f8aebe56535","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NT37YP3GH5QKP90BTYA5P3","author":"impl:1@run-23","body":"Approach for task 1 (exam flag):\n\n- `client/src/storeData.ts`: add `readExamFlag(): boolean` mirroring `readSeed` (no parameter, `read` prefix, so the linter's callback list in `lint-cli.test.ts` is untouched); `createTodosStore` exposes the store when seeded OR when the flag is up.\n- `client/src/Store.tsx`: read the flag once at mount beside the seed; set `window.__TINYAPP_DB__` in the persister factory right after `await getDb()` and `window.__TINYAPP_PERSISTER__` in the `then` callback right after `await persister.load()` resolves, both only under the flag. Hooks stay unconditional: `useCreateSynchronizer` moves into a `SyncLink` child that `StoreLinks` mounts only when the flag is down.\n- Handles are cleared at `Store` mount so a second render in one process (or a page that once held a seed) never reads the previous render's `__TINYAPP_DB__`/`__TINYAPP_PERSISTER__` — the same rule `exposeStore` already applies to `__TINYAPP_STORE__`.\n- `client/src/vite-env.d.ts`: `__TINYAPP_EXAM__?: boolean` beside `__TINYAPP_SEED__` (the two globals a harness sets *into* the page); `__TINYAPP_DB__`/`__TINYAPP_PERSISTER__` beside `__TINYAPP_STORE__` in storeData's `declare global` (the three the page hands *out*).\n- `client/src/sqlite.tsx` is left alone: M2 mocks `getDb`, so the assignment has to live in the persister factory to be observable.\n- `AGENTS.md`: one bullet under `## Key Files` after the seeded-page bullet, naming EXAM, DB, PERSISTER in that order.","created_at":"2026-09-16T19:11:31.286885268Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T19:11:31.288Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7316,"event_uid":"01M2NT9DZ64B794519JDF7RG4S","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":309,"issue_uid":"01M2NSY1V25SJ7BXDZT62TW6CX","issue_short_id":"w6cx","actor":"impl:2@run-23","hlc_physical_ms":1789586094054,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"7ddba1a0500ea92914906ff5723dc743fff1752fb1e35f8846ddab59951fd3a2","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NT9DZ42D1K7TSHPFXX19D3","author":"impl:2@run-23","body":"Approach for task 2 (the persistence move).\n\nPlan, in the order the Context spells the move:\n- `types.ts`: add `PersistenceExamSpec`; `ExamRecord` gains optional `rows` and `domBefore`, `walls` gains optional `persist_ms`/`reload_ms` (all optional so every BASE record still typechecks).\n- `render-move.ts`: `renderHtml`'s `parts.seed` becomes optional; the seed `<script>` is skipped when absent. Nothing else in that function moves, so the seeded output stays byte-identical.\n- `browser.ts`: `connect` gains a persistent listener registry beside its one-shot `once`; `Page` gains an optional `reload()` (arms `Page.loadEventFired`, sends `Page.reload`, awaits it — so the readiness poll after a reload can never read the outgoing document's globals); `Browser` gains an optional `openUrl({url, origin, clock, prelude})` that enables `Fetch` over `*` and answers every `requestPaused` with `continueRequest` for `<origin>/…` and `failRequest BlockedByClient` for everything else. Both new members optional, so the stand-ins in `state-exam.test.ts` and `browser-exam.test.ts` stay assignable.\n- `persistence-move.ts`: `contentOf` (hand-written strip of the stamped `[[tables,hlc,hash],[values,hlc,hash]]` shape, dropping `\\uFFFC`/`null` cells and the rows and tables they empty), `READY_TIMEOUT_MS`/`PERSIST_TIMEOUT_MS`, `runPersistenceExam` and `persistenceExam`.\n- fixture under `test/fixtures/persistence/`, `capture-plugin.ts`'s `EXAM_NO_OPS`, README paragraph.\n\nTwo decisions worth writing down now:\n1. The breach is read inside the readiness poll, not after it. A page that constructs a `WebSocket` at load throws out of its module and therefore never sets `__TINYAPP_PERSISTER__`; checking the breach only after readiness would report M7's ready timeout instead of M4's exact `contract breach: …`.\n2. `app.js` puts everything after the `/` → `/room` redirect inside the `else` branch. At top level the `/` document would keep running and could set `__TINYAPP_PERSISTER__` before the redirect commits, and the exam would then call the pre-redirect document ready.","created_at":"2026-09-16T19:14:54.052656665Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T19:14:54.054Z"}
